---
import ProseLayout from '@/layouts/ProseLayout.astro';

const stages = [
  'Idea',
  'Researching',
  'Source-verified',
  'Outlined',
  'Drafting',
  'Technical review',
  'Editorial review',
];
---

<ProseLayout
  eyebrow="Editorial policy"
  title="Review and approval"
  description="How Runtime Signals reviews, verifies, and authorizes content before it publishes."
  canonicalPath="/editorial-policy"
>
  <div class="workflow-grid" role="list" aria-label="Editorial workflow stages, in order">
    {
      stages.map((stage, i) => (
        <div class="workflow-stage" role="listitem">
          <span class="workflow-stage__mark" aria-hidden="true">
            {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
          </span>
          <span class="workflow-stage__label">{stage}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p>
    That workflow tracks readiness; it does not grant permission to publish. Publication
    authorization is separate and never comes from the content itself. It requires a merged,
    reviewed pull request whose required checks pass, whose CODEOWNERS approval is recorded, and
    whose deployment environment is authorized - captured for the exact commit being built. Nothing
    an author writes in a draft, including a status field, can grant that authorization.
  </p>

  <h2>AI assistance</h2>
  <p>
    LLMs may assist with source triage, metadata extraction, outline suggestions, citation-gap
    detection, and draft critique. No unreviewed AI-generated article is ever published; every
    AI-assisted step is recorded - model, prompt version, inputs, outputs, and the human reviewer's
    decision - and hidden reasoning is never stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    A correction does not erase history. It creates a visible revision note, keeps the article's
    stable URL, and states what changed and why. See <a href="/corrections">corrections</a>.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>

<style>
  .workflow-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(1, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .workflow-stage {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }

  .workflow-stage__mark {
    color: var(--signal);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .workflow-stage__label {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .workflow-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .workflow-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
